{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.CategoricalReeb.SixCanonicalKnotOperators","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.SixCanonicalKnotOperators","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.CategoricalReeb.QReebFlowOnColorCoords"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.boundary_perm_realises_S3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.boundary_perm_realises_S3","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalReeb/SixCanonicalKnotOperators.lean#L152-L168","doc":"**Six canonical knot operators realise $S_3$.**\n\nThe six canonical braid words map to six distinct bijections\nof `ColorSector`, exhausting the six elements of the\nsymmetric group on three sectors.  This is the combinatorial\nboundary-permutation content of\n`prop:six-canonical-knot-operators`; the geometric\nidentification of these permutations with the boundary\nfootprints of the $q$-Reeb flow trajectories (which DOES\nconsume the `QReebFlowOnColorCoords q` class) lives in the\nmanuscript prose, not in this theorem. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:six-canonical-knot-operators","label":"prop:six-canonical-knot-operators","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/six-canonical-knot-operators.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.canonical_braid_count_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.canonical_braid_count_six","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalReeb/SixCanonicalKnotOperators.lean#L143-L150","doc":"The number of distinct boundary permutations realised by the\nsix canonical braids is exactly $6 = |S_3|$.  Together with\n`boundaryPerm_bijective`, this shows the canonical braids\nrealise all six elements of the symmetric group on three\ncolor sectors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.boundaryPerm_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.boundaryPerm_injective","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalReeb/SixCanonicalKnotOperators.lean#L123-L141","doc":"The boundary permutations of the six canonical braids are\npairwise distinct, so the map\n`CanonicalBraid → (ColorSector → ColorSector)` realises an\ninjection into the symmetric group on three sectors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.garside_swaps_red_blue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.garside_swaps_red_blue","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalReeb/SixCanonicalKnotOperators.lean#L116-L121","doc":"The Garside element coincides with the non-adjacent\ntransposition $(rb)$ on the boundary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.threeCycles_are_inverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.threeCycles_are_inverse","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalReeb/SixCanonicalKnotOperators.lean#L107-L114","doc":"The two 3-cycles are inverses of each other on the boundary\ndisc: applying `threeCyclePos` then `threeCycleNeg` returns\nthe identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.boundaryPerm_involution_iff_transposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.boundaryPerm_involution_iff_transposition","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalReeb/SixCanonicalKnotOperators.lean#L89-L105","doc":"The boundary permutation is an involution exactly for the\nidentity element and the three transpositions\n($\\sigma_1$, $\\sigma_2$, garside). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.boundaryPerm_bijective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.boundaryPerm_bijective","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalReeb/SixCanonicalKnotOperators.lean#L69-L87","doc":"`boundaryPerm β` is a bijection on the three-element type\n`ColorSector` for every canonical braid `β`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.CanonicalBraid.boundaryPerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.CanonicalBraid.boundaryPerm","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalReeb/SixCanonicalKnotOperators.lean#L48-L67","doc":"Permutations of the three colour sectors realised on the\nboundary ramified disc.  We encode them as functions\n`ColorSector → ColorSector`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.CanonicalBraid.all_nodup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.CanonicalBraid.all_nodup","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalReeb/SixCanonicalKnotOperators.lean#L45-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.CanonicalBraid.all_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.CanonicalBraid.all_length","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalReeb/SixCanonicalKnotOperators.lean#L42-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.CanonicalBraid.all","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.CanonicalBraid.all","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalReeb/SixCanonicalKnotOperators.lean#L38-L40","doc":"The list of all six canonical braid constructors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.instReprCanonicalBraid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.instReprCanonicalBraid","kind":"instance","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalReeb/SixCanonicalKnotOperators.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.instReprCanonicalBraid.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.instReprCanonicalBraid.repr","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalReeb/SixCanonicalKnotOperators.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.instDecidableEqCanonicalBraid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.instDecidableEqCanonicalBraid","kind":"instance","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalReeb/SixCanonicalKnotOperators.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.CanonicalBraid.threeCycleNeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.CanonicalBraid.threeCycleNeg","kind":"ctor","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalReeb/SixCanonicalKnotOperators.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.CanonicalBraid.threeCyclePos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.CanonicalBraid.threeCyclePos","kind":"ctor","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalReeb/SixCanonicalKnotOperators.lean#L34-L34","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.CanonicalBraid.garside","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.CanonicalBraid.garside","kind":"ctor","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalReeb/SixCanonicalKnotOperators.lean#L33-L33","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.CanonicalBraid.sigma2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.CanonicalBraid.sigma2","kind":"ctor","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalReeb/SixCanonicalKnotOperators.lean#L32-L32","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.CanonicalBraid.sigma1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.CanonicalBraid.sigma1","kind":"ctor","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalReeb/SixCanonicalKnotOperators.lean#L31-L31","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.CanonicalBraid.identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.CanonicalBraid.identity","kind":"ctor","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalReeb/SixCanonicalKnotOperators.lean#L30-L30","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalReeb.CanonicalBraid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalReeb.CanonicalBraid","kind":"inductive","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalReeb/SixCanonicalKnotOperators.lean#L28-L36","doc":"The six canonical braid words on three strands generating $S_3$. ","signatureChunk":0}]}